text:
sarah: FYI partner EdgeWorks just flagged a billing delta — their ledger shows ~0.6 tokens/device extra for a subset of IoT customers. Looks like some minute-level meters were ingested as hourly aggregates. cc @mike @diego

mike: Did they send minute vs hourly flag in payload? we support both but need correct windowing. Can you paste an example event?

sarah: Sent sanitized snippet from EdgeWorks: `{"device_id":"ew-9001","usage":0.01,"units":"minutes","timestamp":"2026-02-28T23:59:00-08:00","window":"2026-02-28T23:00:00-08:00"}` They also had a batch where `units` was `minutes` but window was set to the hour start.

diego: aha — ingestion assumes `window` granularity determines aggregation. If partner sends minute units but sets `window` to hour start we will multiply by 60 in rollup. Need stricter validation: if units=="minutes" then window must be minute-aligned or omit window and use timestamp.

rachel: Could be an SDK bug on their side — older SDK set window to nearest hour for offline devices. Partner says they updated SDK last week but backfilled some older rows.

dmitri: Short-term mitigation: add ingest validation rule that rejects mismatch: `if event.units in ['minutes','seconds'] and (event.window && !is_minute_aligned(event.window)) -> reject with 422`. Also emit a `validation_hint` header in webhook response so partner can backfill correctly.

mike: Good. For already-processed rows we need a safe reconciliation: identify events where units!=hours && recorded_window_is_hour && partner_reported_units_small. Then run backfill to re-attribute usage with `prefer_exact_window=true`. We'll need idempotency keys for partner replay.

partner-bot: Delivery summary EdgeWorks last 48h: 99.2% 200, 0.6% 422 (validation), 0.2% 5xx. Replay endpoint: https://partners.edgeworks.example/replay (internal)

sarah: Proposed action: 1) immediate ingest validation (feature-flagged) -> owner @dmitri 2) run targeted backfill for last 30 days where mismatch detected -> owner @mike 3) auto-credit customers where backfill reduces billed amount, notify partner and customer -> owner @rachel 4) ship partner-facing guidance and SDK snippet -> owner @diego

diego: SDK snippet to suggest to partners (sanitized):

```
// ensure window matches units
const unit = event.units || 'minutes';
if (unit === 'minutes') {
  event.window = roundToMinute(event.timestamp);
}
post('/metering', event);
```

rachel: For credits, suggest policy: auto-credit up to 90 days of delta if discrepancy > $50 or > 2% of monthly bill, require partner confirmation for > 90 days. We should also attach `recon:source=ingest-validation` to credit transactions for audit.

dmitri: Implementing validation in staging now. Example rule (pseudo):

```
function is_minute_aligned(ts) {
  return new Date(ts).getSeconds() === 0 && new Date(ts).getMilliseconds() === 0;
}
if ((event.units === 'minutes' || event.units === 'seconds') && event.window) {
  if (!is_minute_aligned(event.window)) {
    reject(422, {code: 'window_alignment_mismatch', hint: 'window must be minute-aligned for sub-hour units'});
  }
}
```

mike: Backfill plan: scan ledger for events with `units in (minutes,seconds)` AND `window % 3600 == 0` AND partner_id == edgeworks. Create dedupe set using `partner_id|device_id|timestamp|idempotency_key` to avoid double-applying. Run prefer_exact_window transform and generate credit events as needed. ETA: run dry-run tomorrow morning, apply credits after partner sign-off.

sarah: Also add dashboard alerts: `metering.window_alignment_errors`, `billing.delta.edgeworks`, and a weekly report to partnerships with top 5 partners by window-mismatch.

diego: I'll send EdgeWorks an SDK patch link and a short note explaining the validation and replay endpoints. Will ask for a planned replay ETA.

rachel: I'll draft the customer-facing credit email template and hold until dry-run confirms expected credit amounts. cc @sarah for approvals.

dmitri: Feature-flag name `metering.window_alignment_v1`. Canary 5% -> 25% -> 100% if no unexpected 5xx or partner complaints. Add observability on 422 rates.

partner-bot: Ticket created: MET-5482 "EdgeWorks minute-vs-hour window mismatch & backfill" assigned to mike. Link: https://issues.redwood.com/MET-5482

sarah: Great. After credits are applied @diego please ping Partnerships to coordinate partner comms. Closing loop: roadmap item to add unit+window contract validation to the Marketplace docs.

mike: will post dry-run summary to this thread once complete. Thanks everyone.
